1
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:08,310
My...

2
00:00:08,393 --> 00:00:10,517
my strength, it's... it's gone. I...

3
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:12,377
I can't lift...

4
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:13,377
Miseria.

5
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:15,620
Even my vision's blurry. Dammit.

6
00:00:15,980 --> 00:00:16,997
Is this it?

7
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:18,920
I knew this moment would come.

8
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:20,417
But why now?

9
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:22,080
I must press on.

10
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:24,597
Huh? What did...

11
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:25,537
Wait, that's right.

12
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:29,017
Bucciarati and his crew are
trying to get somewhere right now.

13
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:31,394
This could be my chance to learn where.

14
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:34,152
I know the boss is desperate to find out.

15
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:38,333
Um, uh, looks like you could use a hand.

16
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:41,260
Here, I'm happy to
assist you if you'd like.

17
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:43,110
You again?

18
00:00:43,420 --> 00:00:44,773
Why are you still here?

19
00:00:45,180 --> 00:00:46,140
I'll be fine.

20
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:48,051
You should get to safety.

21
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:49,790
I'm sorry.

22
00:00:49,873 --> 00:00:51,777
I don't want to seem pushy or anything.

23
00:00:51,860 --> 00:00:54,625
I just want to make sure
you get across safely.

24
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:57,629
It would put me at ease
if you let me help.

25
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:02,780
I mean, um, only if you don't mind.

26
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:08,280
On second thought, I suppose
I could use a touch of help.

27
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:12,017
Where are we heading, good sir?

28
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:13,000
Not too far.

29
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:15,540
Just the entrance to the Coliseum.

30
00:01:17,740 --> 00:01:20,093
So that's where you're trying to get to.

31
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:33,720
It's a gangster

32
00:01:48,820 --> 00:01:52,760
I'm not sure what I'm saying.

33
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:38,420
And when your body dies, I will never die

34
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:40,897
Hell no!

35
00:02:40,980 --> 00:02:43,760
It's the beginning of the golden ring!

36
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:05,544
Both ways when you're cr - Huh?

37
00:03:05,780 --> 00:03:06,610
What the?

38
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:08,960
His hands are so cold and clammy.

39
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:10,470
I'm sorry.

40
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:13,120
This thing I just tripped on.

41
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:14,800
Is it a guardrail?

42
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:19,900
Hold on a second.

43
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:22,718
Does this mean he can't see anymore?

44
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:26,391
And he didn't even flinch when
that driver honked his horn.

45
00:03:26,580 --> 00:03:28,260
Are his ears busted too?

46
00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:37,037
That gash you have on
your throat. Did I...

47
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:39,708
did I do that to you
in the scuffle earlier?

48
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:42,660
No, that's probably not the case.

49
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:44,797
The wound has already stopped bleeding.

50
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:46,200
That means it's older.

51
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:48,957
How'd you manage to hurt yourself there?

52
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:50,397
He's staring right at it.

53
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:52,040
So he can't still see?

54
00:03:52,420 --> 00:03:54,655
Wait, but it's hidden under my collar.

55
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:57,054
The injury I got from fighting Risotto.

56
00:03:58,160 --> 00:04:00,513
How kind of you to help me pick that up.

57
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:02,500
Crazy mille. I'll take that.

58
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:06,280
Now then, let's get going.

59
00:04:12,180 --> 00:04:13,360
Well, all right.

60
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:15,460
So he can hear me.

61
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:20,500
Still, whatever's ailing him seems way
more complex than just battle wounds.

62
00:04:21,100 --> 00:04:23,080
What's making him act like this?

63
00:04:29,180 --> 00:04:30,160
Oh, shit.

64
00:04:30,460 --> 00:04:32,420
It's Guido Mista. Figures.

65
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:34,417
I knew things were going too well.

66
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:37,537
Should have guessed his friends
wouldn't be too far behind.

67
00:04:37,620 --> 00:04:38,450
Is something the matter?

68
00:04:38,533 --> 00:04:39,363
What's wrong?

69
00:04:39,446 --> 00:04:40,857
We've yet to finish crossing.

70
00:04:40,940 --> 00:04:42,497
I'm sorry. It's just...

71
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:43,840
I need to sit down.

72
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:45,218
My wound opened up.

73
00:04:45,340 --> 00:04:47,164
I'll just be a minute, I swear.

74
00:04:49,040 --> 00:04:50,180
Crap, crap, crap!

75
00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:51,130
He's coming!

76
00:04:51,620 --> 00:04:54,267
Excuse my bluntness,
but I need to get going.

77
00:04:54,420 --> 00:04:56,217
Thank you for all the
help you've given me.

78
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:57,130
No, not now!

79
00:04:57,240 --> 00:04:58,652
I need you to stay here!

80
00:04:59,740 --> 00:05:02,060
I mean, there's another car coming.

81
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:04,157
We can keep crossing once it passes.

82
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:05,070
It's fine.

83
00:05:05,153 --> 00:05:06,737
We've already cleared
that side of the road.

84
00:05:06,820 --> 00:05:08,377
It should be safe to continue.

85
00:05:08,460 --> 00:05:09,290
Come on.

86
00:05:09,373 --> 00:05:10,316
The clock's ticking.

87
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:13,240
Damn it. No. Mista's coming.

88
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:16,100
I'll just have to kill him. Right here.

89
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:17,320
Right now.

90
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:24,080
Oh my goodness.

91
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:26,772
I wonder what that noise could have been.

92
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:31,520
For God's sake, what now?

93
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:34,016
What perplexing game are you playing?

94
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:40,037
Why do you have to call now of all times?

95
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:41,767
Do you want him to find out?

96
00:05:42,020 --> 00:05:43,000
Wait a second.

97
00:05:44,780 --> 00:05:46,839
Would you quit blowing me up, dude?

98
00:05:46,960 --> 00:05:49,297
What's so damn important, you
gotta tell me right this second.

99
00:05:49,380 --> 00:05:51,498
You're gonna blow my freaking cover.

100
00:05:54,380 --> 00:05:56,380
Trish, get back inside the turtle.

101
00:05:56,800 --> 00:05:58,624
We're not out of the woods yet.

102
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:00,697
Please keep a low head for now.

103
00:06:00,780 --> 00:06:01,610
No, wait.

104
00:06:01,693 --> 00:06:02,523
We're not alone.

105
00:06:02,660 --> 00:06:03,601
I can sense him.

106
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:05,620
He's here, I'm sure of it.

107
00:06:06,020 --> 00:06:07,314
That horrible feeling.

108
00:06:07,960 --> 00:06:09,317
There's no mistaking it.

109
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:10,459
It's the same one.

110
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:12,530
Wait.

111
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:13,780
I know you.

112
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:18,960
I finally recognize you.

113
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:22,630
You're...

114
00:06:26,380 --> 00:06:27,210
Trish!

115
00:06:28,260 --> 00:06:30,200
I feel it. He's nearby.

116
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:32,560
The boss is closing in on us.

117
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:34,197
Tell me which way to shoot.

118
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:35,937
Can you tell us exactly where he is?

119
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:38,902
He suddenly appeared, but
I can't pinpoint where.

120
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:40,330
You're safe.

121
00:06:40,620 --> 00:06:42,032
Thank the heavens above.

122
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:43,660
Excellent work.

123
00:06:43,880 --> 00:06:45,857
You've achieved an incredible feat,

124
00:06:45,940 --> 00:06:49,175
although I expect nothing
short of perfection from you.

125
00:06:49,460 --> 00:06:50,340
Rest assured,

126
00:06:50,780 --> 00:06:55,680
Ujarati's eyes may seem to be fixed
on you, but he does not truly see you.

127
00:06:58,500 --> 00:06:59,400
Wait, what?

128
00:06:59,660 --> 00:07:00,800
I don't get it.

129
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:05,840
I possess no insight as to how,
but he's now a reanimated corpse.

130
00:07:06,700 --> 00:07:10,120
He lacks both a pulse and a
working respiratory system.

131
00:07:10,380 --> 00:07:15,145
He's lost use of his eyes, and his eardrums
were ruptured in his fight with Seko.

132
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:20,160
The only thing he's able to see,
Topio, is a rough outline of your soul.

133
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:23,146
The only sound he can
hear are its vibrations.

134
00:07:24,060 --> 00:07:26,457
Physical objects are now invisible to him.

135
00:07:26,540 --> 00:07:30,220
He sees not the car, but the
essence of the driver within.

136
00:07:30,540 --> 00:07:31,720
Trish, talk to me.

137
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:33,497
Did something happen to you?

138
00:07:33,580 --> 00:07:37,840
It just so happens my daughter
and I am at near-identical auras.

139
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:40,900
And for the moment, I
have cloaked you in mine.

140
00:07:41,740 --> 00:07:44,737
Bucciarati presently believes
he is looking at Trish.

141
00:07:44,820 --> 00:07:46,597
You must maintain this illusion.

142
00:07:46,680 --> 00:07:51,260
Let him be your personal guide and have
him take you to this secret meeting.

143
00:07:51,780 --> 00:07:52,610
Trish.

144
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:54,297
I'm so sorry.

145
00:07:54,380 --> 00:07:56,439
I think I got a little lightheaded.

146
00:07:56,540 --> 00:07:57,658
But thank goodness.

147
00:07:57,760 --> 00:07:59,642
I'm relieved to see you're okay.

148
00:07:59,980 --> 00:08:01,140
Yeah, I am.

149
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:04,405
By the way, have you seen
a young man anywhere?

150
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:05,696
Oh yeah, I think so.

151
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:08,337
He looked kind of flustered
and left in a big hurry.

152
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:10,437
We shouldn't worry about him though.

153
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:13,108
Right now we need to
stay focused on moving.

154
00:08:13,460 --> 00:08:14,290
You're right.

155
00:08:14,373 --> 00:08:16,380
I'm sorry, but could...

156
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:19,313
Could you give me a little hand, please?

157
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:21,490
Yes.

158
00:08:21,573 --> 00:08:22,403
I'd be glad to.

159
00:08:33,180 --> 00:08:38,980
In the outskirts of
Napoli, I, I have a house.

160
00:08:39,280 --> 00:08:41,920
It isn't big, but when this is all over,

161
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:47,308
by chance you find yourself needing a
home, you'll be more than welcome there.

162
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:55,880
You know, the area's pretty nice.

163
00:08:56,420 --> 00:08:57,891
Good eats and everything.

164
00:08:58,280 --> 00:08:59,927
And it's close to the beach.

165
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:02,797
I know this has all
been one big nightmare.

166
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:06,060
But I promise, a much
brighter future is waiting.

167
00:09:07,340 --> 00:09:08,300
Sounds nice.

168
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:09,940
But let's stay focused.

169
00:09:10,260 --> 00:09:12,197
Which way do you want me to steer us next?

170
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:14,515
The stairs, please, if you don't mind.

171
00:09:14,660 --> 00:09:15,542
You mean these?

172
00:09:15,660 --> 00:09:17,260
Do not turn around, Dobio!

173
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:18,720
Just keep going.

174
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:21,157
Continue onward as if nothing happened.

175
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:22,122
Someone's here.

176
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:26,800
Behind the stone pillars above,
Someone is watching your every move.

177
00:09:27,420 --> 00:09:30,700
So he really is here to
rendezvous with our foes.

178
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,300
But who could they be?

179
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:34,424
I've zero intel on this person.

180
00:09:34,860 --> 00:09:37,857
How are you so sure that
they're really here, boss?

181
00:09:37,940 --> 00:09:39,517
I mean, even if you're right,

182
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:42,977
how am I supposed to figure out who
they are if I can't turn around?

183
00:09:43,060 --> 00:09:44,680
Look into Butorati's eyes.

184
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:45,917
They will tell you.

185
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,118
Quick, while the reflection's there.

186
00:09:48,560 --> 00:09:49,390
Don't move.

187
00:09:49,660 --> 00:09:51,131
Stay right where you are.

188
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:55,776
Get a step closer to those stairs,
and our agreement will be nullified.

189
00:09:57,160 --> 00:09:58,700
You were right. Crap.

190
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:01,037
Someone's hiding out behind the pillar.

191
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:01,950
I saw him.

192
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:04,240
My name is Bruno Bucciarati.

193
00:10:04,540 --> 00:10:07,717
I've come here on your promise
to reveal the boss's weakness.

194
00:10:07,800 --> 00:10:09,777
I hope you mean to keep your word.

195
00:10:09,860 --> 00:10:10,720
You, I know.

196
00:10:11,100 --> 00:10:12,377
The problem's your friend.

197
00:10:12,460 --> 00:10:14,637
I never said you could bring a plus one.

198
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:17,597
I can't find a shred of
data on them in my records.

199
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:19,033
Of course you wouldn't.

200
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:20,877
Trish here isn't a member of the Familia.

201
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:24,100
In fact, we met barely
more than a few days ago.

202
00:10:24,380 --> 00:10:27,440
But as you can clearly
see, she's batting for us.

203
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:29,700
Trish, you say?

204
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:32,274
To my knowledge, that's a woman's name.

205
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:33,380
Your point?

206
00:10:34,020 --> 00:10:37,140
Merida, I think the jig's
up, boss. Calm down.

207
00:10:37,500 --> 00:10:38,971
Listen, you must respond.

208
00:10:39,780 --> 00:10:42,397
Act furious at him for
doubting your femininity.

209
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:43,310
Do it, Dopeo.

210
00:10:44,860 --> 00:10:48,331
You got some kind of problem
with me being a girl, you pig?

211
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:54,120
My deepest apologies, mademoiselle.

212
00:10:54,400 --> 00:10:56,518
I can't see very well in this light.

213
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:59,240
Is the lady a stand user?

214
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:00,900
Yes, she is!

215
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:02,357
Now, down to business!

216
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:04,657
I think it's about time
you tell us who you are!

217
00:11:04,740 --> 00:11:06,717
Let's talk about why you dragged me here!

218
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:07,630
No, not yet.

219
00:11:07,713 --> 00:11:09,542
I'd like to see her stand first.

220
00:11:10,280 --> 00:11:12,700
And Trish, no sudden movements!

221
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:18,657
I have no data on you, but show me your
stand and I'll get over it. Shit! What now?

222
00:11:18,740 --> 00:11:19,570
Damn it.

223
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:22,697
It appears we're dealing
with a seasoned gladiator.

224
00:11:22,780 --> 00:11:25,839
He's even trying to gauge
a potential enemy's range.

225
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:27,820
Who is this man?

226
00:11:27,980 --> 00:11:29,377
How have I never heard of him?

227
00:11:29,460 --> 00:11:30,460
What's wrong now?

228
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:32,014
Shouldn't be too hard.

229
00:11:32,180 --> 00:11:35,298
Think of it like lifting up
your skirt nice and slow.

230
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:37,960
That's... but how?

231
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:39,740
How does he possess that?

232
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:41,537
That hero...

233
00:11:41,620 --> 00:11:42,700
there's no doubt.

234
00:11:42,980 --> 00:11:44,340
It's the same artifact!

235
00:11:45,820 --> 00:11:48,300
That bloodlust, it's overwhelming.

236
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:51,617
It almost feels like a
dagger racing for my heart.

237
00:11:51,700 --> 00:11:53,620
Where have I felt this before?

238
00:11:55,080 --> 00:11:55,960
Mon Dieu!

239
00:11:57,600 --> 00:11:58,718
Wait, that's right.

240
00:11:58,940 --> 00:12:01,160
I have crossed paths with this man.

241
00:12:01,460 --> 00:12:04,420
He utilized the arrow to
track me down back then.

242
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:06,300
I remember!

243
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:14,600
In Egypt, I unearthed a scattering of
arrows was capable of awakening stands.

244
00:12:16,100 --> 00:12:21,180
I knew simply from beholding them, they
possessed a certain entrancing energy.

245
00:12:21,560 --> 00:12:25,320
An old woman by the name of
Nyaba, who had two right hands,

246
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:28,973
asked that I sell her some in
exchange for their secrets.

247
00:12:29,520 --> 00:12:35,560
In truth, I only needed one, so I sold her
the other five for a very generous sum.

248
00:12:37,620 --> 00:12:41,740
That is when the old bag uttered
something I found truly bizarre.

249
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:49,160
The arrow chooses people, and those
chosen are bound by a curious force.

250
00:12:49,500 --> 00:12:54,380
The 20th century was in its final
decade, and Dio had passed. At the time,

251
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:56,377
my old friend Jotaro Kujo and I were

252
00:12:56,460 --> 00:12:59,342
investigating the arrow
which could awaken Stans.

253
00:13:00,640 --> 00:13:03,977
Word had reached us of a young
boy who had pilfered them,

254
00:13:04,060 --> 00:13:07,240
so he split up and scoured
the globe for the bastard.

255
00:13:07,980 --> 00:13:10,160
Jotaro would search America and Asia,

256
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:16,140
And I, Europe and Africa, I soon managed
to learn the arrow was somewhere in Italy,

257
00:13:16,460 --> 00:13:19,989
hidden in a region suddenly
overcome by drug-related crimes.

258
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:26,057
I focused my search on
a specific region where

259
00:13:26,140 --> 00:13:29,060
juvenile drug deaths had
seen an unusual jump.

260
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:31,972
That's when I knew we were getting close.

261
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:34,630
However...

262
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:41,080
In a few years, my syndicate
